@startuml
title Student single reservation - isolated Browser flow (#892)

actor Student
participant "Web/UI" as UI
participant "HTTP Router" as HTTP
participant "Student CSRF Adapter (design)" as CSRF
participant "Production Session / Authorization Guard" as Guard
participant "Schedule Query" as Schedule
participant "Preview Service" as Preview
participant "Confirm Service" as Confirm
participant "History Query" as History
participant "Reservation / Classification Domain" as Domain
participant "Repository / Transaction Port" as Repo
participant "Audit Port" as Audit
participant "Notification Intent Port" as Intent
database "Isolated D1" as D1

note over UI,D1
  Operator-only seed + test-owned Secure / HttpOnly Session cookie.
  Dedicated HTTPS entrypoint/config; default Worker stays 503.
  No production Provider / Scheduled activation.
end note
Student -> UI: Open /student and choose YYYY-MM
Student -> UI: Request selected month (no published-month list API)
UI -> HTTP: GET /api/me/schedule-months/{month}
HTTP -> Guard: Validate session, role, access, lifecycle
Guard --> HTTP: Resolved student
HTTP -> Schedule: Query month for student
Schedule -> Repo: Read published slots and current state
Repo -> D1: Read
D1 --> Repo: Committed state
Repo --> Schedule: State
Schedule -> Domain: Derive one view per slot
Domain --> Schedule: bookable / reserved_by_me / group_lesson / unavailable
Schedule --> HTTP: Month view
HTTP --> UI: 200 JSON
UI --> Student: Calendar / list; 4 labeled views
note over HTTP,UI: Unpublished/absent month: existing 404; choose another month

Student -> UI: Select slot and request preview
UI -> HTTP: GET /api/auth/student/csrf (same-origin fetch)
HTTP -> HTTP: Check canonical origin / Fetch Metadata
note over HTTP,UI: Origin rejection is 403; stop and retain cookie
HTTP -> CSRF: Exact GET; no query/body
CSRF -> Guard: Resolve this Session
alt valid Session
  Guard --> CSRF: Valid Session; internal context stays server-side
  CSRF -> CSRF: Shared pure session digest with unsafe POST validator
  CSRF --> HTTP: csrfToken + scope: session
  HTTP --> UI: 200 no-store JSON
  UI -> UI: Keep CSRF in memory only
else missing / invalid / expired Session
  CSRF --> HTTP: 401; no preauth token in partial evaluation
  HTTP --> UI: Safe authentication notice; clear Session cookie
  UI --> Student: Stop; return to trusted setup
else resolution unavailable
  CSRF --> HTTP: 503
  HTTP --> UI: Safe error; retain cookie; stop
end

opt CSRF acquisition succeeded

UI -> HTTP: POST /api/me/reservations/preview {slotId}
HTTP -> Guard: Validate this request
Guard --> HTTP: Resolved student
HTTP -> HTTP: Validate Origin / Session CSRF before POST preview
HTTP -> Preview: Preview for student
Preview -> Repo: Read latest slot, month and student reservations
Repo -> D1: Read
D1 --> Repo: Committed state
Repo --> Preview: State
Preview -> Domain: Check eligibility and compute classification effects
Domain --> Preview: Preview result and canonical business snapshot
Preview --> HTTP: Preview view + opaque state token
HTTP --> UI: 200 JSON
UI --> Student: Start/end, classification, all dated before/after changes
UI --> Student: Additional may be reclassified before start; no prices/N

Student -> UI: Explicitly confirm reviewed preview
UI -> UI: Disable duplicate confirm while pending
UI -> HTTP: POST /api/me/reservations {slotId, expectedStateToken}
HTTP -> Guard: Validate this request
Guard --> HTTP: Resolved student + server-internal session context
HTTP -> HTTP: Validate Origin / Session CSRF before POST confirm
HTTP -> Confirm: Confirm for student with internal session context
Confirm -> Repo: Read and guard latest committed state
Repo -> D1: Primary read set + server time T0
D1 --> Repo: State
Repo --> Confirm: State
Confirm -> Domain: Recompute eligibility, snapshot and effects
Domain --> Confirm: Latest result
alt token matches and all guards hold
  Confirm -> Audit: Include booking audit obligation
  Confirm -> Intent: Include confirmation and needed change intents
  Confirm -> Repo: Commit reservation, occupancy, reclassification, audit, intents
  Repo -> D1: batch: capture T, assert read set and Student Write predicate
  Repo -> D1: insert reservation / occupancy, reclassify
  Repo -> D1: insert audit / intents / outbox; final time and session guard
  D1 --> Repo: Committed result
  Repo --> Confirm: Confirmed state
  note over Confirm,Intent: Post-commit delivery responsibility; isolated fake only.
  note over Repo,D1: Intent/outbox commit does not prove Provider delivery.
  Confirm --> HTTP: Reservation, slot and classification changes
  HTTP --> UI: 201 JSON; no delivery result
  UI --> Student: Show confirmed business state
else session / authorization fails
  Repo -> D1: Rollback; fresh Primary session lookup
  Confirm --> HTTP: 401 / 403; lookup failure is 503
  HTTP --> UI: Safe error without latest reservation / slot details
  UI -> UI: Discard confirmation; 401 clears CSRF and stops (403 retains cookie)
else state changed or a booking guard fails
  Repo -> D1: Safe Primary reread after guard failure
  Confirm --> HTTP: 409 safe application error
  HTTP --> UI: Error, optional safe latestSlot
  UI -> UI: Discard expected token / confirmation state
  UI --> Student: Explain change; fresh schedule + preview + human reconfirm
else unavailable / outcome unknown
  Confirm --> HTTP: 503; no automatic write retry
  HTTP --> UI: Safe error; retain cookie
  UI -> UI: Discard token / confirmation state; stop
  UI --> Student: Do not claim success; no automatic Confirm resend
end
note over UI,HTTP
  Lost response discards confirmation and never resends Confirm automatically.
  Safe Schedule/history reread observes current state, not a write retry.
  Month/slot change discards token; stale response cannot enable Confirm.
end note

end

Student -> UI: Open reservation history
UI -> HTTP: GET /api/me/reservations?limit=50
HTTP -> Guard: Validate this request
Guard --> HTTP: Resolved student
HTTP -> History: Query student page
History -> Repo: Read ordered reservations
Repo -> D1: Read
D1 --> Repo: Rows
Repo --> History: Student page
History --> HTTP: items and nextCursor
HTTP --> UI: 200 JSON
UI --> Student: Show reservation, attendance, current classification separately
note over UI,History: nextCursor pages; refresh from first page for current state

@enduml
